{"name":"Angel Food","hex":"#f0e8d9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel food","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Angel food cake, a type of sponge cake made with beaten egg whites and without butter.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see angel,‎ food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel_food"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel food cake","blocks":[{"text":"Angel food cake or angel cake is a type of sponge cake made with egg whites, sugar, and flour, and without oil, baking powder, and various other ingredients common in cakes. It is made in a process of whipping egg whites to a foam, beating in sugar, and folding in flour and more sugar. After baking in a pan with a tube in its center, the cake is hung upside down until cool. The final cake has a slightly chewy texture and white interior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Chocolate_angel_food_cake_with_various_toppings.jpg/330px-Chocolate_angel_food_cake_with_various_toppings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_food_cake","wikidata":"Q29415"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel","wikidata":"Q235113"},{"title":"Food","blocks":[{"text":"Food is any substance that is consumed by an organism for nutritional support. Food usually consists of plant, animal, or fungal origin and contains essential nutrients such as carbohydrates, fats, proteins, vitamins, or minerals. The substance is ingested by an organism and assimilated by the organism's cells to provide energy, maintain life, encourage physical requirements, and support growth. Different species of animals have different feeding behaviours that satisfy the needs of their metabolisms and have evolved to fill specific ecological niches within specific geographical contexts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Good_Food_Display_-_NCI_Visuals_Online.jpg/330px-Good_Food_Display_-_NCI_Visuals_Online.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food","wikidata":"Q2095"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG/250px-Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG/500px-Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG/250px-Angel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAngel_Food_Cake_Pan.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Angel_food_cake_batter_2.jpg/250px-Angel_food_cake_batter_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Angel_food_cake_batter_2.jpg/500px-Angel_food_cake_batter_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki